      "claim": "The image distance $d_i$ for a concave mirror is given by $d_i = \\frac{f d_o}{d_o - f}$, which is a monotonically increasing function of $d_o$ for $d_o > f$.",
      "evidence": "Algebraic rearrangement of the mirror equation $1/f = 1/d_o + 1/d_i$. Differentiating $d_i$ with respect to $d_o$ yields $\\frac{dd_i}{dd_o} = \\frac{-f^2}{(d_o-f)^2} < 0$. This means as $d_o$ decreases (object moves closer), $d_i$ increases (image moves away).",
